# Deferred Backend/Database decisions (locked)

Do not implement these during `FRONTEND_ONLY`. When the user unlocks Backend/Database, use these values without re-asking unless they override in writing.

| Decision | Locked value |
|---|---|
| Default locale (Frontend) | `en` |
| Supported locales | `en` until more are approved |
| Migrations source of truth | `Database/migrations/` (numbered forward-only SQL) |
| Backend migration path | Runner reads `Database/migrations/`; do not duplicate SQL |
| PostgreSQL version | Pin in `Database/infrastructure/postgres.version` (`18.6`) |
| Primary keys | UUID via `gen_random_uuid()` project-wide |
| Structured logger | `pino` (exact pin, JSON, no secrets/PII) |
| API ownership | Native HTTP API lives in `Backend/` |
| Frontend `src/server/` | Next Server Actions / RSC glue only; no second HTTP framework; call Backend with native `fetch` after unlock |
| Rate limit / nonces | PostgreSQL-backed only (no Redis, no in-memory) |
| Auth | HMAC request signing (no Bearer unless later approved) |

Frontend must stay production-ready and performant in isolation during `FRONTEND_ONLY` (budgets, strict TS, Server Components, streaming, no client-side initial fetches).
